  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Alcalde. Type: Asymmetrical Trick-taking. Rules: Alcalde (6 cards, 2 plays/trick) vs 2 Opponents (3 cards each, 1 play/trick). No follow-suit. Goal: Alcalde needs 60 points from Brisca values (A=11, 3=10, K=4, Q=3, J=2).',
    Player: "Welcome to Alcalde. You are either the Mayor (Alcalde) or one of the two opponents trying to take them down. As Alcalde, you'll play TWO cards to every trick, giving you a massive advantage in points—but you need 60 total to win. Opponents, peek at each other's cards and cooperate to keep the Mayor under 60!",
    objective: 'As Alcalde: Score 60+ points to retain the title. As Opponents: Prevent the Alcalde from reaching 60 points to depose them.',
    gameplay: "1. **Trump Exchange**: Any player with the 7 or 2 of trumps can swap it for the face-up 'Life' card if the Life card is a point card (A, 3, K, Q, J). 2. **Cooperation**: The two opponents may peek at each other's hands throughout the game but are forbidden from verbal signaling. 3. **The Trick**: Play is counter-clockwise. Each opponent plays ONE card. The Alcalde then plays TWO cards. 4. **No Follow Suit**: Players can play any card; they are not required to follow the suit of the lead. 5. **Winning Tricks**: The highest trump wins. If no trumps, the highest card of the led suit wins. 6. **Drawing**: After a trick, the winner draws (2 cards for Alcalde, 1 for opponents) followed by others in order.",
    keyRules: [
      "Alcalde plays twice per trick, meaning they control the final 'slap' of the round.",
      'Point Values: Ace=11, 3=10, King=4, Queen=3, Jack=2. Total in deck = 120 points.',
      "The 'Life' card is drawn as the very last card of the deck.",
      'If the Alcalde fails to reach 60, the player to their right becomes the new Alcalde for the next hand.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Exactly 3 players.',
      deck: '40-card Spanish pack. Rank: Ace-3-King-Queen-Jack-7-6-5-4-2 (in order of power/value).',
      equipment: 'Spanish deck (Naipes), scorepad.',
      dealing: "Alcalde deals 3 cards to each opponent and 6 cards to themselves. The next card is the 'Life' card (Trump indicator).",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Trump Exchange**: Any player with the 7 or 2 of trumps can swap it for the face-up 'Life' card if the Life card is a point card (A, 3, K, Q, J). 2. **Cooperation**: The two opponents may peek at each other's hands throughout the game but are forbidden from verbal signaling. 3. **The Trick**: Play is counter-clockwise. Each opponent plays ONE card. The Alcalde then plays TWO cards. 4. **No Follow Suit**: Players can play any card; they are not required to follow the suit of the lead. 5. **Winning Tricks**: The highest trump wins. If no trumps, the highest card of the led suit wins. 6. **Drawing**: After a trick, the winner draws (2 cards for Alcalde, 1 for opponents) followed by others in order.",
